# Neo-Brutalism Funnel Generator

## Surface Model

**Classification: Solid-Border Floating (SBF)**

Brutalism is a hard-surface system. Cards do not dissolve into the background — they declare themselves. The page is white. Every card and section is separated by a thick ink border (4px). Color fills entire blocks, never washes over them. No gradients. No blur. No radius. The border IS the depth system.

- Background: pure white `#FFFFFF`
- Border: near-black `#111827`, always 4px (12px on footer top)
- Accent fills: flat, 100% opaque, one hue per block
- Inversion: one full-page-width section flips to black-on-white — this is the emotional anchor

---

## Token Set

```
--ink:       #111827   (border, body text, inversion bg)
--surface:   #FFFFFF   (page background, most card fills)
--terra:     #DD614C   (primary — terracotta, CTAs)
--gold:      #DAA144   (secondary — amber, warmth)
--emerald:   #16A34A   (success, growth stats)
--orange:    #D97706   (warning, urgency callouts)
--red:       #DC2626   (danger, bold claims)

Synthesized to complete the palette:
--indigo:    #6366F1   (authority, hero)
--rose:      #F43F5E   (trust, testimonials)
--cyan:      #06B6D4   (community, open CTA)
```

**Typography:** Darker Grotesque — 900 for all display and UI labels, 700 for body. JetBrains Mono for code/version strings. Uppercase everywhere in headings and nav. Tight tracking on display (`-0.04em`). Wide tracking on labels (`+0.18em`).

**Borders:** `4px solid var(--ink)` universally. Footer top: `12px solid var(--ink)`.

**Buttons:** Square corners, 4px ink border, hover inverts background ↔ text. `transition: none`. No shadows.

**Decoration:** Ghost numerals (01, 02…) positioned absolute, ink at 8% opacity, aria-hidden. Slash accent `///` in terra color for brand marks.

---

## Required Sections (8 minimum — always include all)

### 1. NAV
Sticky or static header. Logo left (Brand `///` PRO pattern), nav links right. All caps, heavy weight, ink-on-white. Hover inverts to white-on-ink. Bottom border 4px.

### 2. HERO — Asymmetric Split
Left panel (≥55% width): one massive display headline, 3 punchy verbs stacked vertically, last word in an inverted highlight block (terra or ink bg, contrasting text). Right panel: two sub-sections stacked and bordered — upper gets gold fill with headline + body + primary CTA button; lower gets white fill with two stat numbers side by side. Min-height 85vh. Hard vertical border dividing panels.

### 3. FEATURES — Numbered 3-Column
Three equal cells, hard borders between. Each gets a ghost numeral (01/02/03) top-right, a bold feature headline, and a two-sentence body. Cell fills rotate: white → terra → gold. Content sits in the lower half of each cell, ghost numeral floats behind in upper half.

### 4. SOCIAL PROOF — Logo or Metric Bar
Full-width, white bg. Either: a row of company names in caps with slash separators, OR 4 stat blocks (large numeral + label) evenly spaced. Border top and bottom. No cards — this is a horizontal stripe.

### 5. HOW IT WORKS — Process Steps
Numbered 1–4 or 1–3. Two-column alternating layout: step number + label left, description right (or stacked). Hard border rows. One step gets ink inversion (white text on black). Demonstrates the product journey from problem to outcome.

### 6. TESTIMONIALS — Quote Grid
2–3 testimonials. Each is a bordered block with: a large decorative `"` in ghost ink, the quote body in bold, attribution below in label-caps. One testimonial block gets rose or gold fill. Others stay white. If 3 testimonials, use 3-col equal grid. Include a reviewer name and company/role.

### 7. PRICING — Tiered Blocks
2 or 3 tiers in equal columns. Hard borders. Middle/featured tier gets terra or ink fill (inversion). Each tier: name in caps, price in display size, feature list in label-caps with `—` bullets (no icons), CTA button at bottom. Ink-border separator between tiers.

### 8. CTA / ENTERPRISE — Full-Width Inversion
The page's single inversion section. Black background. Subtle grid-line overlay at ~10% white opacity (background-image: linear-gradient grid). One large display headline, colored accent word in gold or terra. Short subline. One ghost-style CTA button (white border/fill, inverts on hover to transparent white text).

### 9. FAQ — Accordion Strip
4–6 questions. Each is a bordered row: question in bold caps left, `+` icon right. Clicking expands the answer. All white bg. No hue fills. Border separates each row. Keeps the page heavy without visual complexity.

### 10. FOOTER
Logo + brand tagline left. Nav links right (Platform / Pricing / Docs / Company). Bottom sub-row: copyright left, Privacy / Terms right. Top border is 12px ink — the heaviest border on the page. White background throughout.

---

## Block Fill Assignment (per section)

| Section | Fill |
|---|---|
| Nav | white |
| Hero left | white |
| Hero right upper | gold |
| Hero right lower | white |
| Feature 01 | white |
| Feature 02 | terra |
| Feature 03 | gold |
| Social proof bar | white |
| Process step (featured) | ink (inversion) |
| Process others | white |
| Testimonial (featured) | rose or gold |
| Testimonial others | white |
| Pricing (featured tier) | terra or ink |
| Pricing others | white |
| CTA section | ink (inversion) |
| FAQ | white |
| Footer | white |

Never place two consecutive hue-fill blocks. Alternating white → hue → white maintains rhythm.

---

## Conversion Psychology

**Emotion sequence the page must carry:**
1. Shock of scale — hero type is overwhelmingly large. First impression is confidence.
2. Specific promise — hero right panel delivers a concrete claim and immediate CTA.
3. Feature proof — numbered cells show what makes this product distinct.
4. Social validation — logos or metrics remove doubt.
5. Process clarity — how it works removes friction.
6. Peer voices — testimonials make it real.
7. Investment framing — pricing tiers present choice, not just cost.
8. Commitment moment — inversion CTA section is the emotional close.
9. Objection handling — FAQ removes remaining resistance.

**Urgency mechanisms (pick one per page):**
- Version stamp in hero stats (`v24.0 / LATEST RELEASE`)
- Metric claim (`99.9% UPTIME SLA`)
- Scarcity in pricing (`LIMITED BETA ACCESS`)

---

## Copy Tone

Brutal. Declarative. Metric-first. Every sentence earns its place or gets cut.

```
✅ "Built for brutal execution."
✅ "Uncompromising tools. No fluff."
✅ "Cut review cycles by 60%."
❌ "We're passionate about helping you grow."
❌ "Unlock the potential of your workflow."
❌ "Seamlessly integrate with your existing tools."
```

Headline structure patterns:
- `VERB. VERB. VERB.` — hero stacked verbs
- `THE [SUPERLATIVE] FOR [AUDIENCE].` — hero right panel
- `READY FOR [STAGE]?` — CTA inversion headline
- `[NUMBER] [METRIC]` — stats always metric-first

---

## Responsive Rules

On mobile (< 768px):
- Hero split → stacked vertically, hero right below hero left
- Feature 3-col → single column, borders become top/bottom only
- Pricing tiers → single column, featured tier first
- FAQ accordion stays accordion

No horizontal scrolling permitted. Touch targets minimum 44×44px.

---

## Anti-Patterns

| Do not | Because |
|---|---|
| Add `border-radius` to anything | Softness breaks the brutalist contract |
| Use `box-shadow` for elevation | Borders define depth here, not shadows |
| Apply gradient fills to cards | Brutalism is flat — one color, solid |
| Smooth button transitions | `transition: none`; the snap IS the interaction |
| Use `font-weight` below 700 in UI | Heavy weight is the typography system |
| Put blur, frost, or glow on surfaces | Explicitly anti-brutalist |
| More than 2 consecutive hue-fill sections | Destroys the white-hue-white rhythm |
| Place text on low-contrast backgrounds | Verify all ink-on-color pairs at WCAG AA |
| Use emoji as icons | Square bordered SVG containers only |
| Skip the inversion section | It is the page's emotional anchor — required |

---

